**Usage:**

```tsx
// Basic — uses built-in fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary
  fallback={(error, reset) => (
    <div>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// With external error reporter
<ErrorBoundary onError={(err, info) => Sentry.captureException(err, { extra: info })}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Key design decisions:**

- `getDerivedStateFromError` — captures error synchronously, triggers fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` — logs to console + fires optional `onError` prop (Sentry/Datadog hook)
- `reset` resets state to `null`, re-rendering children fresh — this is the retry
- `fallback` prop lets callers fully own the UI; omit it for the built-in card
- Class component required — React error boundaries can't be function components
